      "why": "Seq 1 anchors the conversation and seq 3 parks on the gap, so the ordering state is live. The server then sends seq 1 again (a drain/live overlap or a lost ack): it is below the anchor and this client already handled it, so it is not handed over again, and it is acknowledged again, because the earlier dispatch is the proof. Seq 2 then releases 2 and 3 in order."
